' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing how MODULES and PROJECT FILES
' are traversed and processed while performing Act steps (episodes).
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with minimal partitions,
' one or two decision points, and explanatory notes instead of nested detail.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - Module & Project File Processing during Act Steps

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Scan the project folder;

if (Non-recursive mode?) then (yes)
  note right: Skip module recursion; only this project's files are processed.
else (no)
  :Find modules in this project;
  if (Modules found?) then (yes)
    :Recursively scan and process each module;
    note right
      Modules can run one after another,
      or in parallel when multi-threading
      is enabled. Each module is scanned
      the same way as the top-level project.
    end note
  endif
endif

:Collect this project's own files;
note right
  Module directories are excluded here,
  and remaining files are filtered by the
  configured match rules and exclusions.
  If nothing matches, the project folder
  itself is processed instead.
end note

:For each collected file;

:Run the act's episodes for this file;
note right
  See "Episodes Act Processing" for how
  episodes are selected and ordered.
  A file's processing can stop early if
  the act signals the task should end.
end note

:Record the result;

note right
  This flow repeats for every collected file,
  unless processing was stopped early.
end note

stop

legend right
  * Modules are discovered from the project layout and processed
    recursively, each one scanned the same way as the top level.
  * Non-recursive mode limits work to the current project only.
  * Files inside module folders are not processed again as
    "parent" files - they belong to their own module's pass.
  * Stopping early during a file skips any remaining files.
endlegend

@enduml
